le><![CDATA[‘My grandpa’s name was Dan Singh’: Fox anchor Alec Nolan hits back at DHS post targeting ‘Mr Singh’]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134009467.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/my-grandpas-name-was-dan-singh-fox-anchor-alec-nolan-hits-back-at-dhs-post-targeting-mr-singh/articleshow/134009467.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/my-grandpas-name-was-dan-singh-fox-anchor-alec-nolan-hits-back-at-dhs-post-targeting-mr-singh/articleshow/134009467.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T17:57:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134009843,imgsize-125742.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Why did armed people come looking for Destiny's son? Kick streamer recalls frightening incident]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134002546.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Kick streamer Destiny recounted terrifying experiences involving armed individuals near his home. He vividly described an alarming encounter where people brandished rifles and interrogated him about his son. Moreover, Destiny shared the ordeal of being swatted, leading to police unexpectedly storming his residence. These chilling incidents have profoundly shaped his view on online threats and harassment, affecting his family members as well, including his son and mother.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/why-did-armed-people-come-looking-for-destinys-son-kick-streamer-recalls-frightening-incident/articleshow/134002546.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/why-did-armed-people-come-looking-for-destinys-son-kick-streamer-recalls-frightening-incident/articleshow/134002546.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T17:25:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134002648,imgsize-390781.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A Pennsylvania family bought a 12-acre farm in 1916; 110 years and four generations later...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134008734.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Maple Acres Farm remains Plymouth Township's last working farm, a testament to agricultural heritage.  The McKeown family has preserved thirty acres of land since nineteen sixteen.  This farm now serves as a community market and pick-your-own destination.  It thrives by adapting its business model to suburban surroundings.  Community support and family dedication ensure its continued operation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-pennsylvania-family-bought-a-12-acre-farm-in-1916-110-years-and-four-generations-later-it-has-grown-to-30-acres-and-is-the-townships-last-working-farm/articleshow/134008734.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-pennsylvania-family-bought-a-12-acre-farm-in-1916-110-years-and-four-generations-later-it-has-grown-to-30-acres-and-is-the-townships-last-working-farm/articleshow/134008734.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T17:56:09+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134009772,imgsize-186486.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[15-year-old found alive on overturned fishing boat after going missing off Alaska]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134003668.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A 15-year-old boy was rescued after being found clinging to an overturned 18-foot fishing boat about four miles east of St. Lawrence Island, Alaska. The Coast Guard had launched a search for three missing boaters after the vessel failed to return. Two other boaters were found dead in the water and taken to Nome with the survivor.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-15-year-old-was-missing-after-an-18-foot-fishing-skiff-failed-to-return-near-alaska-rescuers-found-him-clinging-to-the-capsized-vessel-about-4-miles-offshore/articleshow/134003668.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-15-year-old-was-missing-after-an-18-foot-fishing-skiff-failed-to-return-near-alaska-rescuers-found-him-clinging-to-the-capsized-vessel-about-4-miles-offshore/articleshow/134003668.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T18:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134004401,imgsize-175576.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[17-year-old turns cancer treatment decisions into a 72-card game for students]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134002182.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-daniel-zhang-the-17-year-old-san-diego-cancer-researcher-who-turned-treatment-decisions-into-a-72-card-game-and-has-helped-bring-stem-education-to-1500-children/articleshow/134002182.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-daniel-zhang-the-17-year-old-san-diego-cancer-researcher-who-turned-treatment-decisions-into-a-72-card-game-and-has-helped-bring-stem-education-to-1500-children/articleshow/134002182.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T18:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134004140,imgsize-24908.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Tax startup CEO allegedly faked CPA credentials and company revenue to raise $13.3 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134007898.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Federal agents arrested a former startup executive in Florida just as she was set to board a cruise ship. She is accused of swindling over $13 million from venture capital funds by falsely portraying herself as a licensed CPA while fabricating revenue reports. It is alleged that the funds were misappropriated for personal luxuries, including an extravagant wedding, leaving investors with substantial financial setbacks after her company's abrupt downfall.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/tax-startup-ceo-allegedly-faked-cpa-credentials-and-company-revenue-to-raise-13-3-million-investors-lost-everything-as-funds-paid-for-a-home-tesla-and-caribbean-wedding/articleshow/134007898.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/tax-startup-ceo-allegedly-faked-cpa-credentials-and-company-revenue-to-raise-13-3-million-investors-lost-everything-as-funds-paid-for-a-home-tesla-and-caribbean-wedding/articleshow/134007898.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T17:29:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134008513,imgsize-146715.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A Taylor Swift fan helped describe 12 new insect species; 4 species named after her music and life]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134007888.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A new genus of Australian insects has been named Swiftiephylus after singer Taylor Swift.  Four new species within this genus also bear names inspired by her music.  These pale yellow and cream-colored insects were collected between 1995 and 2004.  Their discovery highlights the vast undocumented insect diversity remaining globally.  This naming brings attention to insect conservation and scientific discovery.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/a-lifelong-taylor-swift-fan-helped-describe-12-new-insect-species-she-named-a-new-genus-and-four-species-after-the-singer-and-her-albums/articleshow/134007888.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/a-lifelong-taylor-swift-fan-helped-describe-12-new-insect-species-she-named-a-new-genus-and-four-species-after-the-singer-and-her-albums/articleshow/134007888.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T17:26:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134008174,imgsize-1101094.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Newport mansion revives 1500s staircase craft with mortise-and-wedge joinery]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133970182.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-newport-mansion-is-being-restored-with-a-staircase-technique-dating-to-the-1500s-instead-of-modern-exposed-fasteners-craftsmen-lock-the-wooden-steps-together-with-mortises-and-wedges/articleshow/133970182.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-newport-mansion-is-being-restored-with-a-staircase-technique-dating-to-the-1500s-instead-of-modern-exposed-fasteners-craftsmen-lock-the-wooden-steps-together-with-mortises-and-wedges/articleshow/133970182.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T17:26:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133970402,imgsize-850468.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘He has no business being in our country’: Indian-origin man charged in crash that killed US woman]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134002470.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/he-has-no-business-being-in-our-country-indian-origin-man-charged-in-crash-that-killed-us-woman/articleshow/134002470.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/he-has-no-business-being-in-our-country-indian-origin-man-charged-in-crash-that-killed-us-woman/articleshow/134002470.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T16:42:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134003885,imgsize-52740.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Giant reed came to California in the 1820s; now it crowds out native plants and fuels wildfires]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134000282.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Giant reed, a plant native to eastern Asia, was introduced to California in the 1820s for roofing material and erosion control. It has since become an invasive weed, growing rapidly and forming dense stands that displace native plants. In Southern California’s Santa Ana River Basin, arundo infestations have almost tripled fire fuel loads and also increased pressure on water resources.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-the-1820s-giant-reed-reached-california-for-erosion-control-two-centuries-later-it-crowds-out-native-plants-and-has-doubled-or-tripled-wildfire-fuel-in-parts-of-southern-california/articleshow/134000282.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-the-1820s-giant-reed-reached-california-for-erosion-control-two-centuries-later-it-crowds-out-native-plants-and-has-doubled-or-tripled-wildfire-fuel-in-parts-of-southern-california/articleshow/134000282.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T16:53:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134003068,imgsize-137996.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Deer fled 64% of the time from human voices, but soon ignored them]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133966453.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/in-2023-researchers-tested-human-voices-predator-calls-dog-barks-and-flashing-lights-on-elk-and-deer-in-british-columbia-human-shouts-scared-them-most/articleshow/133966453.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/in-2023-researchers-tested-human-voices-predator-calls-dog-barks-and-flashing-lights-on-elk-and-deer-in-british-columbia-human-shouts-scared-them-most/articleshow/133966453.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T16:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133966579,imgsize-95878.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Elk Herd Roaming Farther: Reintroduced West Virginia animals test new range; tourism tours expand]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133951548.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[West Virginia's elk restoration initiative is flourishing, with the herd expanding to around 130 individuals alongside numerous native calves. Elk are venturing into new territories, showcasing a robust population increase. This revival not only highlights the animals' successful reintroduction into their habitat but also boosts local tourism, marking a remarkable triumph in wildlife conservation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/west-virginias-restored-elk-herd-is-finally-roaming-farther-heres-how-a-conservation-comeback-is-changing-the-landscape/articleshow/133951548.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/west-virginias-restored-elk-herd-is-finally-roaming-farther-heres-how-a-conservation-comeback-is-changing-the-landscape/articleshow/133951548.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T16:47:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133951614,imgsize-1152239.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Who is Rohit Rohit? Man who stalked woman for months before fatal Sacramento shooting]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134007223.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/who-is-rohit-rohit-man-who-stalked-woman-for-months-before-fatal-sacramento-shooting/articleshow/134007223.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/who-is-rohit-rohit-man-who-stalked-woman-for-months-before-fatal-sacramento-shooting/articleshow/134007223.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T17:17:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134007907,imgsize-67217.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1974, Australian ranger proposed wildlife bridge; 52 years later, it opened over motorway]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133961826.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An innovative wildlife crossing, born from an Australian park ranger's fifty-two-year-old vision, has finally been realized. Cawleys Bridge has been modified to facilitate safe passage for important wildlife across a bustling motorway. This enhancement allows species like koalas to navigate between vital habitats such as Heathcote National Park and Garrawarra State Conservation Area. Future wildlife monitoring will assess usage patterns and guide subsequent conservation projects.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/in-1974-an-australian-ranger-proposed-turning-a-service-bridge-into-a-wildlife-corridor-52-years-later-it-opened-over-a-motorway-carrying-40000-vehicles-a-day-reconnecting-two-national-parks/articleshow/133961826.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/in-1974-an-australian-ranger-proposed-turning-a-service-bridge-into-a-wildlife-corridor-52-years-later-it-opened-over-a-motorway-carrying-40000-vehicles-a-day-reconnecting-two-national-parks/articleshow/133961826.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T16:20:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133961949,imgsize-2273322.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Abandoned Idaho bridge gets a second life as wildlife crossing]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134003932.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An abandoned bridge over Interstate 90 in Osburn, Idaho, was repurposed as a wildlife crossing. This initiative was championed by a local truck driver who witnessed numerous animal collisions. Conservation groups and state officials collaborated to transform the unused structure into a safe passage. Trail cameras confirmed deer regularly using the bridge, avoiding the dangerous interstate. The bridge, though temporary, successfully provided a vital crossing for animals.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-idaho-bridge-sat-unused-for-56-years-after-mining-cut-off-its-road-in-2025-it-reopened-for-wildlife-where-nearly-75-animals-had-been-struck-within-two-miles-in-a-decade/articleshow/134003932.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-idaho-bridge-sat-unused-for-56-years-after-mining-cut-off-its-road-in-2025-it-reopened-for-wildlife-where-nearly-75-animals-had-been-struck-within-two-miles-in-a-decade/articleshow/134003932.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T15:51:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134003952,imgsize-117210.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Could kill us all': Another AI employee quits, sounds alarm over safety]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134003102.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/could-kill-us-all-another-ai-employee-quits-sounds-alarm-over-safety/articleshow/134003102.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/could-kill-us-all-another-ai-employee-quits-sounds-alarm-over-safety/articleshow/134003102.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T15:55:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134004096,imgsize-706774.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[17.83-acre private Georgia island hits market for $2.5M]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134002125.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/a-17-83-acre-private-georgia-island-made-up-of-seven-separate-parcels-has-hit-the-market-for-2-5-million-allowing-a-buyer-to-keep-it-whole-or-potentially-build-seven-homes/articleshow/134002125.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/a-17-83-acre-private-georgia-island-made-up-of-seven-separate-parcels-has-hit-the-market-for-2-5-million-allowing-a-buyer-to-keep-it-whole-or-potentially-build-seven-homes/articleshow/134002125.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-10T15:40:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134002340,imgsize-1092034.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1883, Hawaii introduced Guinea grass; 143 years later, it grows 9 feet and yields 9,000 seeds]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134001443.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Once celebrated for its grazing benefits, Guinea grass has become a formidable threat to Hawaii's delicate ecosystems. Since its introduction in the 19th century, it has proliferated, reaching impressive heights. This resilient perennial can generate thousands of seeds and rebound swiftly from fires, exacerbating wildfire risks by providing ample fuel across the islands. Its growth pattern serves as a stark reminder of the lasting ecological impact of imported plant species.]]></description>